<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to offer three-year bonds of HUF 17.5 bln.</title>
<headline>Hungary to offer three-year bonds of HUF 17.5 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will offer three-year government bonds of the 2000/F series, worth a total 17.5 billion forints at an auction on July 31, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Monday.</p>
<p>    First day of interest    July 7, 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   Aug 24, 2000</p>
<p>    Bonds on offer	    17,500 million forints</p>
<p>Maximum average annual</p>
<p>     yield			    18.14</p>
<p>Average annual yield</p>
<p>     at last auction (July 3)   17.14 pct</p>
<p>    Minimum price		   96.64 pct</p>
<p>Average price</p>
<p>     at last auction		98.77 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 16.00 percent, payable semi-annually starting from February 24, 1998.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
